### Preserve the cursor offset for one-step undo (12/14)

**Severity:** `medium`

The expansion path moves left for a cursor marker, but undo currently retains only the replacement text and deletes its full length from that interior position. For `ab$|$cd`, that requests four Backspaces after moving left twice; the delete range includes text before the replacement and leaves its suffix. Move back to the end of the inserted text before undo erases it. Keep this movement before either insertion backend, and abandon the operation if movement fails or the destination is no longer authorized. Apply every part of this group together.

